# Browsers the build must support. This app's users often keep older phones,
# so the floor sits well below Angular's default (recent versions only).
# Raise it only after analytics confirms those devices are gone.
# Safari/iOS: 14.1/14.5 is the lowest the build tooling (esbuild) can target
# since Angular 19; every iPhone that ran iOS 14 can install 14.5+.
# Builds warn that these browsers are outside Angular 22's official support;
# that is expected. esbuild still lowers the syntax for them, while missing
# APIs are polyfilled in src/legacy-polyfills.ts and missing CSS features get
# fallbacks in src/_material-compat.scss. The `oldest-supported-browser` e2e
# project checks the app in a Chromium that behaves like iOS 14.5.
Chrome >= 80
ChromeAndroid >= 80
Edge >= 88
Firefox >= 78
Safari >= 14.1
iOS >= 14.5
Samsung >= 12
